            "text": "Since 2019, Adyar"
          }
        },
        "h": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Two potters,\none small studio",
            "size": "h0"
          }
        },
        "t": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Kolam & Clay started in a rented garage in Adyar with one second-hand wheel and a kiln we had to share with a neighbour's generator. Meera had trained in ceramics in Pondicherry. Arjun had just quit software testing after a weekend class he couldn't stop thinking about.</p><p>We still make everything ourselves. Meera carves and paints the kolam patterns; Arjun mixes the glazes and looks after the kiln. Between us we throw about forty pieces a week.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "We make the pieces we wanted on our own kitchen shelves.",
            "author": "Meera & Arjun"
          }
        },
        "f": {
          "type": "founders",
          "settings": {
            "names": "Meera Raghavan & Arjun Selvam",
            "role": "Founders and potters",
            "portrait": "shopify://shop_images/Joyful_Pottery_Studio_Collaboration.png"
          }
        }
