    "kolam": {
      "type": "studio-story",
      "blocks": {
        "e": {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Why kolam"
          }
        },
        "h": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "A line drawn every morning",
            "size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "t": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Across Tamil Nadu, women draw kolam at the doorstep before sunrise, a single looping line around a grid of dots, in rice flour so ants and birds can eat it by evening. It's made to be lived with, then made again.</p><p>That's how we think about pottery. Our mugs and plates are meant to be used every day, chipped a little, loved a lot.</p>"
          }
        },
